    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the `frai` CLI. The issue was in how the `gate` command delegated to the `frai-gate` subprocess.\n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen using commander.js's variadic argument capture (`[args...]`), the action handler only receives positional arguments, not flags like `--ci`. This meant `frai gate init --ci` was passing only `['init']` to the subprocess, missing the `--ci` flag entirely.\n\n**The Fix:**\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755) to capture all arguments after `gate` directly from `process.argv` instead of relying on commander's variadic array. This ensures both positional arguments and flags are properly passed through to the frai-gate subprocess.\n\n**Testing:**\n\u2713 Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2713 Tested `frai gate init --ci` in a fresh directory\n\u2713 Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created correctly",
